From a4e9b7be465cd44bd2299b7d3a9c79d9b8c4340d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhouyllll <xuezhou28@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:38:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/34] arch/arm64/rk3576: add polled SPI master driver (SPI4)

Synopsys DesignWare SSI, Rockchip variant (rockchip,rk3066-spi).
Register layout differs from stock DW SSI: data ports are split
(TXDR 0x400 / RXDR 0x800) and CTRLR0 bitfields are rearranged.

Only SPI4 is implemented: it is the sole general-purpose SPI routed
to the 40-pin header on KICKPI-K7; the other three are disabled in
the base dtb with no external pins.

Chip select uses GPIO4_A5 rather than the controller's native CS,
matching the vendor cs-gpios.  NuttX splits chip select into
independent select/deselect calls that must hold for a whole
transaction, which native per-frame CS cannot do.  SER bit0 is still
asserted -- with SER clear the controller emits no clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FBQkQQFX3kTDP3AzvLzDGx
---
