From 74c7a2d63af08db7e49610ddf66b0f19f9abccc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhouyllll <xuezhou28@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:06:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/34] arch/arm64/rk3576: add MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY receiver

First stage of the camera capture path.  This is different hardware
from rk3576_dcphy.c, not a direction flag on it: the display side is a
Samsung DCPHY transmitter, this is an Innosilicon receiver, and the two
register sets do not overlap.  Reference implementations are
phy-rockchip-samsung-dcphy.c and phy-rockchip-csi2-dphy-hw.c
respectively.

The dtb exposes csi2_dphy0..5 but there are only two physical blocks
(0x2b030000 and 0x2b070000); index < 3 uses the first, >= 3 the second.
The board's sensor is on csi2_dphy3.

THS-SETTLE is the one value that must track the link rate: the receiver
waits it out after a lane leaves LP before it starts sampling.  Getting
it wrong yields data with corrupt packets rather than no data at all,
so the two symptoms must not be confused.  A rate past the end of the
table falls back to the top entry and says so -- silently running the
fastest setting produces exactly that corrupt-packet symptom, which is
hard to trace back to an out-of-range rate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FBQkQQFX3kTDP3AzvLzDGx
---
 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/Kconfig          |  13 +
