From bc209e7ff21891788202f179086f89fe52d03e78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhouyllll <xuezhou28@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:27:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/34] arch/arm64/rk3576: add MIPI CSI-2 host controller

Second stage of the capture path, and the first point in it that can be
observed at all.  The sensor can only be confirmed over I2C and the
D-PHY has no status registers, so until now nothing could answer
whether data was actually on the wire.  PHY_STATE shows per-lane
stopstate and clock-lane activity; ERR1/ERR2 count SoT, ECC and CRC
failures.

That distinction matters because "no data" and "data arriving
corrupt" both look like a blank screen but need opposite next steps.
The status helper reports which one it is rather than printing raw
values.

Verified on hardware: with the sensor streaming, PHY_STATE reads
0x2f0 and both error registers are zero; with the sensor in standby it
reads 0x0f.  The changing bits identify [3:0] as per-lane stopstate and
bit 9 as clock-lane HS activity.  The vendor driver never reads this
register, so the bit meanings come from that comparison rather than
from documentation -- and zero errors alone would not have settled it,
since no packets also produces no errors.

Gate selection uses the register/bit from the CRU driver table, not the
dt-bindings clock index: the binding header here disagrees with the
board dtb about index 379, so indices are not trustworthy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FBQkQQFX3kTDP3AzvLzDGx
---
 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/Kconfig          |  12 +
 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/Make.defs        |   4 +
 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/rk3576_csihost.c | 301 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/rk3576_csihost.h |  55 +++++
 4 files changed, 372 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/rk3576_csihost.c
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/src/rk3576/rk3576_csihost.h

diff --git a/arch/arm64/src/rk3576/Kconfig b/arch/arm64/src/rk3576/Kconfig
index fc86aa91..034fbcbc 100644
